---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>Boomerang - Untamed Weapons</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav class="nav">
			<div class="container">
				<a href="/" class="logo">UNTAMED</a>
				<div class="nav-links">
					<a href="/rules">Rules</a>
					<a href="/quick-reference">Quick Reference</a>
					<a href="/character">Characters</a>
					<a href="/bestiary">Bestiary</a>
					<a href="/gm-guide">GM Guide</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main>
			<div class="container">
				<div class="breadcrumb">
					<a href="/character">← Back to Character Creation</a>
				</div>

				<header class="page-header">
					<div class="weapon-icon"><img src="/weapons/Boomerang.png" alt="Boomerang" /></div>
					<h1>Boomerang</h1>
					<p class="subtitle">Skirmisher / Tempo</p>
					<div class="stat-badges">
						<span class="stat-badge">+1 INS</span>
						<span class="stat-badge">+1 DEX</span>
					</div>
				</header>

				<article class="content">
					<section class="weapon-section">
						<h2>Overview</h2>
						<p>The Boomerang is a finesse weapon built for agile, midrange hunters who thrive on timing and spatial awareness. Every throw is a risk–reward cycle: the longer you keep your rhythm, the deadlier your return. The throw is only half the technique. The catch is where the fight turns — and masters of the Wayback use motion itself as a weapon, hitting twice before enemies can react.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="weapon-section">
						<h2>Weapon Attributes</h2>
						<div class="attributes-grid">
							<div class="attribute-card">
								<h3>Tags</h3>
								<ul>
									<li>Thrown (30/90 ft)</li>
									<li>Returning</li>
									<li>Ranged</li>
									<li>Finesse</li>
									<li>Two-Handed (light)</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div class="attribute-card">
								<h3>Attack &amp; Save Stat</h3>
								<p class="formula">Instinct</p>
								<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">Save DC: 10 + INS mod + proficiency</p>
								<p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Disadvantage beyond 30 ft.</p>
							</div>
							<div class="attribute-card">
								<h3>Basic Throw</h3>
								<p><strong>1 Stamina:</strong> d20 + INS + proficiency vs AR → weapon damage on hit.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</section>

					<section class="weapon-section highlight">
						<h2>Core Mechanic — Wayback Catch</h2>
						<p>Every hit is an invitation to catch and return. Keep moving and the boomerang rewards you — stand still and you're leaving damage on the table.</p>
						<div class="mechanic-details">
							<h3>The Loop</h3>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Throw (Action, 1 STA):</strong> Make a Boomerang attack vs AR. On a <strong>hit</strong> — attempt a Wayback Catch.</li>
								<li><strong>Wayback Catch:</strong> Roll d20 + INS + proficiency vs <strong>DC 13</strong>. Success: the boomerang snaps back to your hand — you may re-throw as a <strong>Fast Action (1 STA)</strong> this turn.</li>
								<li><strong>Movement bonus:</strong> If you moved <strong>≥10 ft</strong> since your last throw, the return throw has <strong>advantage</strong> and deals <strong>+1 damage die</strong>.</li>
								<li><strong>Per-turn limit:</strong> Up to <strong>2 Wayback catches per turn</strong> — at most: Action throw → FA return → FA second return.</li>
								<li><strong>Double-catch reward:</strong> If both catches succeed in the same turn, the second return throw costs <strong>0 Stamina</strong> and deals <strong>+1 Power Die</strong> on hit.</li>
								<li><strong>Skirmish Rhythm:</strong> You may move freely between the throw and the catch — normal opportunity attacks apply unless a technique says otherwise.</li>
							</ul>

							<h3>If the Catch Fails</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>The boomerang returns to your hand but you can't re-throw this turn.</li>
								<li>You can still act normally — the catch check doesn't cost an action.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<section class="weapon-section">
						<h2>Damage Dice per Tier</h2>
						<table class="damage-table">
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th>Tier</th>
									<th>Damage Dice</th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								<tr><td>Tier 1</td><td>1d6 + INS</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Tier 2</td><td>1d8 + INS</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Tier 3</td><td>2d6 + INS</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Tier 4</td><td>2d8 + INS</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Tier 5</td><td>3d6 + INS</td></tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>
						<p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--leaf-green);">The return throw's damage comes from movement — advantage and the +1 die reward hunters who stay mobile.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="weapon-section">
						<h2>Techniques by Tier</h2>

						<div class="technique-card">
							<div class="technique-header">
								<h3>T1 — Ricochet Step</h3>
								<div class="technique-cost">Passive</div>
							</div>
							<p>You've learned to flow with the throw — your footwork feeds the arc.</p>
							<ul>
								<li>After a successful hit, you may move up to <strong>10 ft</strong> before attempting your Wayback Catch. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks from creatures you hit this turn.</li>
								<li>Your <strong>first successful Wayback Catch</strong> each turn gives <strong>+1 to hit</strong> on the immediate return throw.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="technique-card">
							<div class="technique-header">
								<h3>T2 — Split Return</h3>
								<div class="technique-cost">2 Stamina • Action</div>
							</div>
							<p>Curve the throw to clip two targets in one motion — or thread a large creature's body and a vulnerable part in the same pass.</p>
							<p><strong>Effect:</strong> Throw in a curved path that hits <strong>two targets within 15 ft of each other</strong>, or <strong>two body parts on one Large or larger creature</strong>. Make a separate attack roll against each.</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Counts as a single throw for Wayback purposes — make one catch check after both attacks resolve.</li>
								<li><strong>If both attacks hit:</strong> Wayback DC reduced by 2 for this catch, and you regain <strong>1 Stamina</strong> at the end of your turn.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="technique-card">
							<div class="technique-header">
								<h3>T3 — Threaded Arc</h3>
								<div class="technique-cost">Passive</div>
							</div>
							<p>Your throws curve around cover and through gaps that should be impossible. Nothing hides from the arc.</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Your throws ignore <strong>all cover</strong> — half, three-quarters, and full. You may target creatures you cannot directly see as long as you know their approximate location.</li>
								<li>Your Wayback Catch DC is permanently reduced by 2 (<strong>DC 13 → DC 11</strong>). Split Return's both-hit bonus stacks on top (DC 11 → DC 9).</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="technique-card">
							<div class="technique-header">
								<h3>T4 — Momentum Flow</h3>
								<div class="technique-cost">Passive</div>
							</div>
							<p>Your rhythm is unbreakable. Catches fuel movement, movement fuels catches.</p>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Bigger payoff:</strong> When both catches succeed in the same turn, the second return throw deals <strong>+2 Power Dice</strong> (up from +1).</li>
								<li><strong>Skate Catch:</strong> When you attempt a Wayback Catch, you may move up to your <strong>full Speed</strong> as part of the attempt. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks from creatures you hit this turn.</li>
								<li><strong>Safety net (1/turn):</strong> You may reroll one failed Wayback Catch.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="technique-card">
							<div class="technique-header">
								<h3>T5 — Cyclone Return</h3>
								<div class="technique-cost">4 Stamina • Action</div>
							</div>
							<p>You unleash a multi-pass storm — the boomerang spirals out and back, shredding everything in its path.</p>
							<p><strong>Effect:</strong> Throw in a <strong>20-ft line</strong>, hitting all enemies in the path (weapon damage each). Then attempt a Wayback Catch:</p>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>First catch success:</strong> The boomerang returns along the same line — repeat the line attack and add <strong>+1 damage die</strong> to every hit.</li>
								<li><strong>Second catch success:</strong> A third pass (outbound or sweeping curve) adds another <strong>+1 damage die</strong> (max +2 dice total from Cyclone).</li>
								<li>All throws inside Cyclone Return cost <strong>0 Stamina</strong> and don't count against your normal per-turn Wayback limit.</li>
								<li><strong>Failing a catch ends the sequence immediately.</strong></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<section class="weapon-section playstyle">
						<h2>Weapon Playstyle</h2>
						<div class="playstyle-grid">
							<div class="playstyle-card strengths">
								<h3>Strengths</h3>
								<ul>
									<li>Movement is damage — advantage and bonus dice reward hunters who stay mobile</li>
									<li>Two-catch baseline means three attacks per turn is achievable from T1</li>
									<li>Split Return contributes part break progress without sacrificing damage</li>
									<li>Threaded Arc removes positioning restrictions entirely at T3</li>
									<li>Cyclone Return is a genuine multi-target nuke at T5</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div class="playstyle-card weaknesses">
								<h3>Weaknesses</h3>
								<ul>
									<li>Catch only triggers on a hit — miss the throw and the loop stalls</li>
									<li>Lower per-hit damage without chaining successful catches</li>
									<li>Stamina-hungry at full output (3 STA for a full double-catch turn)</li>
									<li>High-AR targets blunt momentum — hitting is the prerequisite for everything</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>
		</main>

		<style>
			* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
			:root {
				--forest-dark: #1a2e1a; --forest-green: #2d5016; --moss-green: #4a7c2f;
				--leaf-green: #6b9d3a; --amber: #d4a257; --earth-brown: #5c4033;
				--cream: #f5f1e8; --text-light: #e8e4d8;
			}
			body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; background: var(--forest-dark); color: var(--text-light); line-height: 1.7; min-height: 100vh; }
			.container { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem; }
			.nav { background: var(--forest-green); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber); padding: 1rem 0; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100; }
			.nav .container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; max-width: 1200px; }
			.logo { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 900; color: var(--amber); text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: 0.2rem; }
			.nav-links { display: flex; gap: 2rem; }
			.nav-links a { color: var(--cream); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; transition: color 0.3s; }
			.nav-links a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
			.breadcrumb { padding: 2rem 0 1rem; }
			.breadcrumb a { color: var(--leaf-green); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
			.breadcrumb a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
			.page-header { padding: 2rem 0 3rem; text-align: center; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
			.weapon-icon { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.weapon-icon img { width: 540px; height: 540px; object-fit: contain; }
			.page-header h1 { font-size: 3rem; color: var(--amber); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
			.subtitle { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--leaf-green); font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.stat-badges { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; }
			.stat-badge { padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--moss-green); color: var(--amber); border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1rem; }
			.content { padding-bottom: 4rem; }
			.weapon-section { background: var(--forest-green); padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; margin-bottom: 2rem; border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown); }
			.weapon-section.highlight { border-color: var(--amber); background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest-green) 0%, var(--moss-green) 100%); }
			.weapon-section h2 { color: var(--amber); font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
			.weapon-section h3 { color: var(--leaf-green); font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
			.weapon-section p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.weapon-section ul { margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.weapon-section li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
			.attributes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
			.attribute-card { background: var(--forest-dark); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown); }
			.attribute-card h3 { color: var(--amber); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.attribute-card p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
			.attribute-card ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; }
			.attribute-card li { padding-left: 1.5rem; position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
			.attribute-card li:before { content: "▸"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--amber); }
			.formula { background: var(--moss-green); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 4px solid var(--amber); font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-weight: 600; color: var(--amber); text-align: center; }
			.mechanic-details { background: var(--forest-dark); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 1rem; }
			.damage-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--forest-dark); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
			.damage-table th, .damage-table td { padding: 1rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--earth-brown); }
			.damage-table th { background: var(--moss-green); color: var(--amber); font-weight: 600; }
			.damage-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
			.technique-card { background: var(--forest-dark); padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 2px solid var(--amber); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
			.technique-header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--earth-brown); }
			.technique-header h3 { color: var(--amber); font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 0; }
			.technique-cost { background: var(--moss-green); padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--amber); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; }
			.playstyle-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
			.playstyle-card { background: var(--forest-dark); padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown); }
			.playstyle-card.strengths { border-color: var(--leaf-green); }
			.playstyle-card.weaknesses { border-color: #c74440; }
			.playstyle-card h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--amber); }
			.playstyle-card ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; }
			.playstyle-card li { padding-left: 1.5rem; position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
			.playstyle-card li:before { content: "▸"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--amber); }
			@media (max-width: 768px) {
				.nav .container { flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
				.nav-links { gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
				.page-header h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
				.weapon-section { padding: 1.5rem; }
				.technique-header { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; }
			}
			html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
